  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: certificate chains through compromised eMudhra\n     intermediate CA keys are accepted by the ssl module\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-115557.patch: install a verify callback on\n       every SSLContext that rejects any certificate whose public key\n       (SHA-256 of the SubjectPublicKeyInfo) is on a built-in denylist of the\n       compromised eMudhra intermediate CA keys, in Modules/_ssl.c and the new\n       Modules/_ssl/distrusted_spki.h, so such chains fail verification even\n       while the system trust store still has the root; adds the upstream\n       regression test to Lib/test/test_ssl.py.\n     - CVE-2026-115557",
